Z||000000||msweldon||10-16-2000||01:04 PM||||Does anyone know the part # or where I can locate a replacement for the large black trim just below the windshield where the windshield washer spindles come through. <P>I'm trying to locate a source for a new one and not a boneyard.  I've polished and painted mine as long as possible, but its just getting too old and cracked.<P>thanks,<BR>marc||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-16-2000||01:26 PM||||The only source of new I know of would be a GM/pontiac dealer.<P>Polished and painted? I just use a plastics cleaner or "total shine" on mine. The total shine took off all the old wax and crap on it. That alone was a tremendous improvement. ARmorall and that type thing work good if you want a gloss to it. If it's oxidized a scrub with a soft 3M Scotch Brite pad helps allot.<P>They call the stuff total shine but it works really well on the semi flat trim, unlike waxes that make it look like hell. I also use it to help the look of my faded lugage rack. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-16-2000||04:41 PM||||From the 22P manual<P>Description            part number<BR>Shrd top vent (84/85)  20559921<BR>shrd top vent (86/88   10074271<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
